Nobody remembers installing it because nobody did. Google put it there through a system update, the kind your phone does on its own overnight. One morning it was just sitting in your apps, set up to read your pictures.

Google says the scanning happens on the phone itself and calls it a safety feature. Maybe so. But you were never asked, never told in plain words, and never given the choice before it arrived.

Your photo roll is the most private thing on your phone. Family, grandkids, screenshots of bills and letters. A company should have to knock before it moves in there.

Be honest… did you know this app was on your phone before this post?

